From 478d9ae5e872c853bd862dad5c10c0bf52a3f478 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:53:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sidebar): group project presentation across gateways
 [daveey]

Projects sharing a trimmed case-folded name now share a presentation header,
filter/dismissal identity, and entered view while retaining each original
backend node's placement and expansion pipeline. Primary metadata and new-chat
routing prefer the window gateway. Each entered member retains its own git
and worktree route and group reads do not supersede one another.

Do not rederive owner maps, hidden counts, preview membership or Home. Existing
store-merged row multiplicities and foreign hydration limitations are retained.
The prior placement-reimplementation approach (#3724) is superseded by this
presentation-only seam under Decision234504/operator14:00.

Proof: real-base differential overview/member/nested/placement oracles and
24 seeded singleton DOM digest cells; source-only RED/GREEN; mounted 96-cell
navigation matrix and same-path grouped git bridge local/studio controls.

